    "result_text": "The only test class is `AcceptanceTest` (the others are a base class and a helper), and it passes. The build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a `bulkSignupWarning` flag to owner responses: **true when more than 80 owners have already been created for the current business day, otherwise false.**\n\nSince the flag depends on a repository count (not on any single `Owner` entity), it can't come from the MapStruct mapper \u2014 I compute it in the responder steps instead:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`BulkSignup.java`** (new helper) \u2014 `warningFor(OwnerRepository)` counts owners whose `registrationDate` equals the current business day (weekend rolled forward, matching `ResolveRegistrationDate`) and returns `count > 80`. This shares the same per-day accumulation path as the existing `CheckDailyLimit` rule (which hard-caps at 100), so the warning fires in the 81\u201399 band before the cap.\n\n3. **Responders** \u2014 `RespondWithOwner` (GET), `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (POST), and `RespondWithOwnerUpdated` (PUT) now inject `OwnerRepository`, set `dto.setBulkSignupWarning(BulkSignup.warningFor(...))` after mapping, and send the DTO.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"bulkSignupWarning\", ignore = true)` so MapStruct leaves the field for the responder to populate (no unmapped-target warning).\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold` (the false branch) and the full suite pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
